==== handle_elite_abilities
" Back-compat entry point: attaches the elite behavior-tree brain (once) and
" ends. The brain drives ability selection each tick, replacing the old
" hand-rolled loop. Kept as a named label because //spawn, the GM add-ability
" comms, and a2x set_special all schedule it by name.
metadata: ```
brain:
  SEQ Elite Abilities:
    - elite_bt_gate
    - elite_bt_charge
    - elite_bt_activate
```
    ->END if ELITE_ID is None
    # elite_brain_attach, not brain_add: the tree has to go FIRST (the root Select
    # stops at the first child that succeeds, so an elite already chasing something
    # would starve it), and it has to be idempotent on ITS OWN flag. The guard here
    # used to be "does this ship have any brain at all", which handed every elite that
    # arrived with a movement brain an ability set it could never use.
    elite_brain_attach(ELITE_ID, brain)
    ->END


=== elite_bt_gate
" Gate node: succeed only when this elite should consider an ability - not
" tag-suppressed, an enemy is near, and no ability is already running. Also
" detects a just-finished ability to emit its end signal and clear state.
metadata: ```
type: brain/npc
```
    so = to_object(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    yield fail if so is None

    # An ability is mid-run: hold until its task finishes, then emit end + clear.
    elite_task = get_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_TASK", None)
    if elite_task is not None:
        yield fail if not elite_task.done()
        ability = get_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_ACTIVE_ABILITY", None)
        # The cooldown is set HERE, from the ability's own `cool_down:` metadata scaled
        # for this crew, rather than by each ability's last line. One place, and an
        # ability that ends early - or is killed with its ship - still gets one.
        if ability is not None:
            set_timer(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, f"{ability}_cooldown", elite_ability_cool_down(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ability))
        signal_emit("elite_ability_end", {"ELITE_ID": BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ability": ability})
        set_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_TASK", None)
        set_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_ACTIVE_ABILITY", None)

    # Tag torpedo suppression (timer set in damage/destroy.mast; True when unset).
    # A charge in progress is called off rather than left standing: the tell Science is
    # reading has to stop being true the moment it stops being true.
    if not is_timer_finished(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "tag_suppression"):
        elite_charge_abort(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
        yield fail

    # Elites only use powers when near non-friendly ships.
    stuff = broad_test_around(so, 18000, 18000, 0xF0)
    nearest_target = closest(so, stuff - role(so.side))
    if nearest_target is None:
        elite_charge_abort(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
        yield fail
    yield success


=== elite_bt_charge
" Choose an ability, then charge it in the open.
"
" This is the node the ticket asked for: the elite commits to what it is about to
" do some time BEFORE it does it, and says so, so a Science officer has something
" to notice and to call out. How long it charges is the ability's own `warm_up:`,
" scaled for the crew opposite (elite_ability_warm_up). An ability that declares
" no warm-up succeeds the moment it is chosen, exactly as every ability did before.
metadata: ```
type: brain/npc
```
    pending = get_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_PENDING_ABILITY", None)

    if pending is None:
        all_abilities = elite_get_non_engine()
        ready = []
        for ab in all_abilities:
            if not has_role(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, ab):
                continue
            if is_timer_finished(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, f"{ab}_cooldown"):
                ready.append(ab)

        yield fail if len(ready) == 0

        pending = random.choice(ready)
        set_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_PENDING_ABILITY", pending)
        # Returns 0 when the ability declares no warm-up - fire this same tick.
        yield success if elite_charge_begin(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, pending) <= 0
        yield fail

    # Some abilities are worth calling off while they charge. Warp is: it used to
    # bail out of its own warm-up loop when its target got close, and that loop is
    # gone, so the reason to bail is metadata now (`abort_if_target_within:`).
    abort_within = elite_ability_meta(pending, "abort_if_target_within", 0)
    if abort_within:
        # default=0, not a bare read: the engine answers None for a field it never
        # set, and the comparison below would raise on a real bridge.
        target_id = get_data_set_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "target_id", default=0)
        if target_id:
            if sbs.distance_id(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, target_id) <= abort_within:
                elite_charge_abort(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
                yield fail

    yield fail if not is_timer_finished(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "elite_warmup")
    yield success


=== elite_bt_activate
" Action node: launch the ability this elite spent its warm-up committing to. The
" task runs the ability sequence; the gate holds the tree until it completes.
metadata: ```
type: brain/npc
```
    ab = get_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_PENDING_ABILITY", None)
    yield fail if ab is None

    all_abilities = elite_get_non_engine()
    elite_label = all_abilities.get(ab)
    if elite_label is None:
        elite_charge_abort(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
        yield fail

    elite_task = task_schedule(elite_label, data={"ELITE_ID": BRAIN_AGENT_ID})
    set_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_TASK", elite_task)
    set_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_ACTIVE_ABILITY", ab)
    set_inventory_value(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ELITE_PENDING_ABILITY", None)
    # The charge is spent. Take the tell down BEFORE the ability runs - what Science
    # reads next is the ability's own doing, not a leftover countdown.
    elite_charge_clear(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)
    signal_emit("elite_ability_start", {"ELITE_ID": BRAIN_AGENT_ID, "ability": ab})
    yield success




